              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तुला — tulā — \"a balance, scales\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tulā is built on the root √tul, \"to lift up, weigh\" (MW): a balance lifts things to weigh them (CDIAL 5886). MW compares the root with Latin tulī, \"I carried\", an inherited Indo-European root. It is also the sign Libra, the Scales."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
