        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "daṇḍa is a Rigvedic word for \"stick, club\" (CDIAL 6128). MW relates it to Greek dendron, \"tree\", and to Sanskrit dāru, \"wood\", but CDIAL thinks it probably non-Aryan and finds no support for the Greek comparison, so the origin is not settled. It later also meant \"punishment\", the stick that rules."
            }
          ]
        },
